    "evilTwinSafeWhatIs": "Most home routers broadcast the same Wi-Fi name (SSID) over 2.4 GHz, 5 GHz and sometimes 6 GHz. Your phone sees them as separate access points even though they're one device. Mesh systems work the same way — every node uses one shared name.",
