    "howPingStabilizerWorksTitle": "How Ping Stabilizer works",
    "@howPingStabilizerWorksTitle": {},
    "stabilizerExplainerSubtitle": "On-device, no remote servers, free.",
    "@stabilizerExplainerSubtitle": {},
    "whatItDoesTitle": "What it does",
    "@whatItDoesTitle": {},
    "whatItDoesBullet1": "Establishes a local VPN tunnel on your device — no traffic leaves through any third-party server.",
    "@whatItDoesBullet1": {},
    "whatItDoesBullet2": "Routes DNS queries to the fastest resolver (1.1.1.1, 8.8.8.8, 9.9.9.9, …) measured live.",
    "@whatItDoesBullet2": {},
    "whatItDoesBullet3": "Watches latency / jitter every second and warns you when a spike persists, optionally cycling the tunnel to break a sticky bad path.",
    "@whatItDoesBullet3": {},
    "whatItDoesBullet4": "Uses an EWMA filter (recent samples weighted heavier) so it reacts to real degradation, not single-packet noise.",
    "@whatItDoesBullet4": {},
    "whatItDoesNotTitle": "What it does NOT do",
    "@whatItDoesNotTitle": {},
    "whatItDoesNotBullet1": "It cannot make your ISP's route to the game server physically shorter — no on-device app can.",
    "@whatItDoesNotBullet1": {},
    "whatItDoesNotBullet2": "It does not replace a paid VPN/relay service like ExitLag or WTFast (those route via their own servers; this is local-only).",
    "@whatItDoesNotBullet2": {},
    "whatItDoesNotBullet3": "Multi-path \"first-wins\" send across Wi-Fi + cellular is on the roadmap (Phase 2) and currently disabled.",
    "@whatItDoesNotBullet3": {},
    "risksAndThingsToKnowTitle": "Risks & things to know",
    "@risksAndThingsToKnowTitle": {},
    "risksBullet1": "Android shows a key icon while the tunnel is active — that is normal and required by the system.",
    "@risksBullet1": {},
    "risksBullet2": "Only one VPN can run at a time. If you have another VPN app connected, this will refuse to start.",
    "@risksBullet2": {},
    "risksBullet3": "A persistent live notification (current ping + Stop / Cycle buttons) stays in the shade while the tunnel runs — that is your in-game HUD; do not swipe it away.",
    "@risksBullet3": {},
    "risksBullet4": "On Xiaomi/MIUI, OnePlus/OxygenOS and similar skins, you may need to allow Torcav under Settings → Notifications and Settings → Battery → No restrictions, or the OS will silently hide the notification.",
    "@risksBullet4": {},
    "risksBullet5": "DNS auto-switch will change which resolver answers your queries while the tunnel is on. That switch reverts when you stop the stabilizer.",
    "@risksBullet5": {},
    "risksBullet6": "Battery use is small (~3-5%/hr in our tests) but non-zero — turn it off when you're done playing.",
    "@risksBullet6": {},
